//www.cbc.ca/news/politics/foreign-interference-public-safety-1.7345861","title":"Foreign interference inquiry probes CSIS warrant application that lingered on minister's desk","publisher":"CBC News","date":"2024-10","kind":"other","added_by":"nonevents_deep_dive_2026-10-29","source_layer":"records"},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/democracy-watchdog-to-file-conflict","title":"Democracy Watchdog To File Conflict Complaint Against Liberals And Bill Blair On Michael Chan Warrant","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-31","kind":"samcooper","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true,"added_by":"nonevents_deep_dive_2026-10-29"},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/mounties-should-probe-criminal-obstruction","title":"Mounties Should Probe Criminal Obstruction in Bill Blair's Office Warrant Delay, Says Former Senior CSIS and RCMP Officer","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-11-18","kind":"samcooper","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true,"added_by":"nonevents_deep_dive_2026-10-29"},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/top-trudeau-aides-deny-involvement","title":"Top Trudeau Aides Deny Involvement In 54-Day Delay of CSIS Warrant Targeting Liberal Powerbroker Michael Chan","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-15","kind":"samcooper","id":"samcooper-substack-2024-10-15-top-trudeau-aides-deny-involvement","note":"Paywalled: only the headline and free preview were read.","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/how-i-developed-sources-for-the-prc","title":"How I Developed Sources For The PRC Election Interference Story: Wilful Blindness 3rd Edition Excerpt","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-12","kind":"samcooper","id":"samcooper-substack-2024-10-12-how-i-developed-sources-for-the-prc","note":"Paywalled: only the headline and free preview were read.","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/minister-blairs-successor-cautions","title":"Minister Blair's successor cautions against political influence in CSIS warrant approvals","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-10","kind":"samcooper","id":"samcooper-substack-2024-10-10-minister-blairs-successor-cautions","note":"Paywalled: only the headline and free preview were read.","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/the-warrant-involved-high-ranking","title":"“The warrant involved high-ranking members of your party. Isn’t that why you delayed it?”: Commission Lawyer to Bill Blair’s Former Aide","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-09","kind":"samcooper","id":"samcooper-substack-2024-10-09-the-warrant-involved-high-ranking","note":"Paywalled: only the headline and free preview were read.","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true},{"url":"https://www.thebureau.news/p/warrant-delayed-by-minister-blairs","title":"Warrant Delayed by Minister Blair's Office Involved Case Concerning PM Trudeau's Office, Intel Sources Allege","publisher":"The Bureau (Sam Cooper)","date":"2024-10-07","kind":"samcooper","id":"samcooper-substack-2024-10-07-warrant-delayed-by-minister-blairs","note":"Paywalled: only the headline and free preview were read.","source_layer":"samcooper","paywalled":true}],"summaries":{"records":"The foreign interference inquiry heard that a CSIS warrant application sat in then-Public Safety Minister Bill Blair's office for 54 days after it went to his chief of staff Zita Astravas; Blair testified he signed it the day he first saw it (CBC). The Bureau reported the warrant concerned former Ontario minister Michael Chan and that Democracy Watch would file a conflict complaint.","samcooper":"The Bureau reports that a CSIS warrant concerning Liberal powerbroker Michael Chan sat in Public Safety Minister Bill Blair's office for 54 days in 2021; Blair's former chief of staff Zita Astravas denied delaying it at the Hogue Commission (per The Bureau)."},"layer_ids":{"nonevents":["ent_event_csis_warrant_approval_delayed_2021"],"samcooper":["ent_event_csis_warrant_approval_delayed_2021"]},"added_by":["nonevents_deep_dive_2026-10-29"],"_intro":{"intro":"The foreign interference inquiry heard that a CSIS warrant application sat in then-Public Safety Minister Bill Blair's office for 54 days after it went to his chief of staff Zita Astravas; Blair testified he signed it the day he first saw it (CBC). The Bureau reported the warrant concerned former Ontario minister Michael Chan and that Democracy Watch would file a conflict complaint. Event status: Delayed (shown as a hollow star): the sources describe it as expected but delayed. Expected: Ministerial approval of a CSIS warrant application within the usual time (CSIS officials testified it took much longer than usual) (2021). On the map: 5 link(s) (2 verified, 3 reported). Also named in the sources (not placed at the event): Rob Stewart, Michael Chan. How it links across the map, in date order: Democracy Watch lobbied Innovation, Science and Economic Development Canada (1997-09-04) (before this event) [verified; records]; Public Safety Canada contracted National Cyber-Forensics and Training Alliance, $79,100 (2013-11-20) (before this event) [verified; records]; Canadian Security Intelligence Service took part in CSIS threat-reduction measure against Indian intelligence networks scaled down (2017) (before this event) [reported; records]; Democracy Watch testified on House of Commons Standing Committee on Access to Information, Privacy and Ethics (2020-08-10) (before this event) [verified; records]. In the Surveillance and investigative-technology vendors to federal security buyers timeline: just before, Royal Canadian Mounted Police contracted BlackBerry Limited, $15,820 (2020-12-17) (2020-12-17); just after, Royal Canadian Mounted Police contracted Incite Experiential Design Inc. (RMUS Canada), $538,551 (2022-01-05) (2022-01-05). In the Digital forensics tool vendors and resellers (federal) timeline: just before, Royal Canadian Mounted Police contracted NicheVision Forensics LLC, $83,000 (2020-07-08) (2020-07-08); just after, Canada Border Services Agency contracted Nuix, $55,880 (2022-01-31) (2022-01-31). In the OSINT and social-media analytics vendors (federal) timeline: just before, Royal Canadian Mounted Police contracted Maltego Technologies, $392,790 (2020-05-29) (2020-05-29); just after, Royal Canadian Mounted Police contracted Data Centre Intelligence Inc., $1.27 million (2022-10-24) (2022-10-24). It also sits in 1 more network timeline(s). What else on the map connects here: lobbying 201 (1997 to 2026); contracts, grants or programs 17 (2013 to 2024); bills or votes 4 (2020 to 2026); hollow-star events 10 (1997 to 2024); spy-tech items 26 (2005 to 2025); Breach items 1; other events 14 (2015 to 2024); charge or investigation records 2; networks: Surveillance and investigative-technology vendors to federal security buyers, Digital forensics tool vendors and resellers (federal), OSINT and social-media analytics vendors (federal), Surveillance-technology firms registered to lobby federal security institutions. Layers: bloodmoney, breach, events, wiretap."},"_next":[{"label":"See where it fits: Surveillance and investigative-technology vendors to federal security buyers","tour_id":"tour_net_spytech_federal_security_vendors"},{"label":"See where it fits: OSINT and social-media analytics vendors (federal)","tour_id":"tour_net_spytech_osint_social_media"},{"label":"See it in the Surveillance and investigative-technology vendors to federal security buyers timeline","view":"timeline","network":"net_spytech_federal_security_vendors"},{"label":"See it in the Digital forensics tool vendors and resellers (federal) timeline","view":"timeline","network":"net_spytech_forensic_tools"},{"label":"Open the lobbying around it (201)","view":"map"}],"_ov":[[4925,"co_cited","ent_event_csis_warrant_approval_delayed_2021","ent_person_michael_chan",["https://www.the